## Utils vs database helpers

Use this rule when adding or moving code shared between **web (including client components)**, **core**, and **database**.

### Put in `@sokosumi/utils`

- **Pure TypeScript**: types, constants, parsers, formatters with no I/O
- **No Prisma**, repositories, or `server-only` dependencies
- **Any module imported from** `'use client'` components or other client bundles
- **Cross-app product vocabulary** used in UI and server code alike (e.g. billing plan name unions, `parseSelfServeSubscriptionPlanName`, credit conversion helpers in `credit.ts`)

Export from `packages/utils/src/index.ts` and colocate tests under `packages/utils/src/__tests__/`.

### Keep in `@sokosumi/database`

- **Repositories** and all Prisma access
- **Helpers that need a transaction client** or load rows from the database
- **Domain resolution** that combines DB state (e.g. `resolveOrganizationBillingPlan`, enterprise contract lifecycle, credit-bucket scope with org membership)

Server code may import these from `@sokosumi/database/helpers`.

### Import rules

| Consumer | Import from |
| -------- | ----------- |
| Client components, shared UI utils | `@sokosumi/utils` |
| Server Components, server actions, API routes, database helpers | `@sokosumi/utils` for pure shared bits; `@sokosumi/database/helpers` for DB-backed helpers |

**Do not** import `@sokosumi/database/helpers` from client code. The helpers barrel re-exports server-only modules (Prisma, repositories). A single value import can pull the whole graph into the Next.js client bundle and fail the build (`node:module`, etc.).

**Do not** add new `@sokosumi/database/helpers/<subpath>` exports only to dodge the barrel—move the shared surface to utils instead.

### No cross-package re-exports

- **`@sokosumi/database/helpers` must not re-export** symbols from `@sokosumi/utils`. Import shared pure helpers from `@sokosumi/utils` at each call site (client or server).
- Follow [avoid-re-exports.mdc](./avoid-re-exports.mdc) for apps and other packages—no passthrough modules or duplicate type definitions.

### Example (billing plan names)

- **Utils**: `SelfServeSubscriptionPlanName`, `OrganizationBillingPlanName`, `parseSelfServeSubscriptionPlanName` → `packages/utils/src/organization-billing-plan-names.ts`
- **Database**: `OrganizationBillingPlan`, `resolveOrganizationBillingPlan` → `packages/database/src/helpers/organization-billing-plan.ts` (imports plan-name types/parser from `@sokosumi/utils`)

### Checklist before merging

1. New shared pure helper → utils + export from `index.ts` + vitest in utils
2. Client or `subscription-plan-utils`-style module → no `@sokosumi/database/helpers` import
3. `pnpm --filter @sokosumi/utils build` when database or apps depend on new utils exports
4. `pnpm web:build` (or `pnpm build`) after touching client import paths

See also [shared-packages.mdc](./shared-packages.mdc) for general deduplication workflow.
